From: Q2 Navidrome maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ash: acknowledge read interruption before checking pending traps

BusyBox 1.38 can retain bb_got_signal after a trap has handled the signal.
The read builtin then repeatedly receives EINTR with no pending ash trap.
Consume the notification on the returned EINTR path, before testing
pending_sig, with a compiler barrier between the two accesses. A new
signal after the test remains visible to the next poll. Other users of
bb_got_signal, including line editing, retain their existing semantics.

Reported upstream: https://github.com/vda-linux/busybox_mirror/issues/16
Downstream report: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/23745

--- a/shell/ash.c
+++ b/shell/ash.c
@@ -14652,16 +14652,26 @@
 	 * to jump out of it.
 	 */
  again:
 	INTOFF;
 	r = shell_builtin_read(&params);
 	INTON;
 
 	if ((uintptr_t)r == 1 && errno == EINTR) {
+#if ENABLE_FEATURE_EDITING
+		/* Consume the notification which interrupted this read before
+		 * deciding whether an ash trap is pending. A handled signal can
+		 * leave this flag set after dotrap() cleared pending_sig.
+		 * Do not clear it after the pending_sig test: a new signal there
+		 * must remain visible to the next read/poll.
+		 */
+		bb_got_signal = 0;
+		barrier();
+#endif
 		/* To get SIGCHLD: sleep 1 & read x; echo $x
 		 * Correct behavior is to not exit "read"
 		 */
 		if (pending_sig == 0)
 			goto again;
 	}
 
 	if ((uintptr_t)r == 2) /* -t SEC timeout? */
